### 6.3 STEP 3 — the exec CLI surface, and a command the wiki promises that this build does not have

`tools/tb qmark tb277 secmode1304 u2 115200 'crypto ' 'crypto secure-mode ' 'crypto
secure-mode-selftest ' 'show secure-mode ' 'show p'` — raw: `work/q-exec-D.out`, then
`work/q-exec-D2.out`, `work/q-exec-D3.out`.

    awplus# crypto ?
      key          Key management
      pki          Public Key Infrastructure (PKI) Commands
      random       Generate a random byte sequence
      secure-mode  Secure mode

    awplus# crypto secure-mode ?
      delete  Remove key material

    awplus# crypto secure-mode delete ?
      hostkey  Hostkey

    awplus# show secure-mode ?
      |  Output modifiers
      >  Output redirection
      >>  Output redirection (append)
      <cr>

Three findings:

1. **The exec-mode and config-mode `crypto secure-mode` are different commands.** In exec it is
   *not* complete — `?` offers no `<cr>`, only `delete`, which in turn offers only `hostkey`.
   `crypto secure-mode delete hostkey` is a **destructive** exec command ("Remove key
   material"). **Not run.** Recorded so nobody reads the exec form as a harmless synonym of the
   config one.
2. `show secure-mode` offers `<cr>` and nothing but output modifiers — a pure display command,
   which is why §6.1 could be run freely.
3. 🔴 **`crypto secure-mode-selftest` does not exist on this build.**

       awplus# crypto secure-mode-selftest ?
       % Unrecognized command

   The dispatch asked that this command not be run unless it was first proven read-only, and
   that if read-only could not be established it be skipped and the skip reported. The question
   is now moot in the strongest possible way: **the parser does not recognise the command at
   all**, in exec mode, in normal mode, on `sin_x96056-20261019-27`. Note what the wiki claims
   for it, in the `show post` row of *Secure-mode Differences*:

       'show post' | Normal: show results from file system checks
                   | secure-mode: show results from post and cryptographic algorithms/modules
                   |              same cryptographic info can be shown using
                   |              'crypto secure-mode-selftest' in EXEC mode

   Two readings are consistent with the measurement and this run cannot separate them: either
   the command is registered only while secure mode is enabled, or it is not implemented on the
   x960. **Either way it was not run, and the reason is a `% Unrecognized command` from the DUT,
   not a judgement call.** Deciding between the two readings is part of the attended window
   (§8).

RESULT: surface quoted; the one risky command named in the dispatch turns out not to exist.

