12. WHAT THIS RUN ESTABLISHED, AND WHAT IT DID NOT
---------------------------------------------------

**Established, measured on swi_d:**
- secure mode is **disabled** on the DUT, and the configuration agrees with the display;
- the feature's CLI **exists on this platform**: `crypto secure-mode` / `no crypto secure-mode`
  are complete global-configuration commands, so TPS row 226 is not a paper claim;
- `crypto secure-mode-selftest` is **not recognised** in exec on this build;
- `crypto secure-mode delete hostkey` is the only exec form, and it is destructive;
- `show post` in normal mode prints exactly the wiki's Normal column — six file-system checks,
  all OK, no cryptographic information — so the instrument for the secure-mode comparison is
  identified and its normal-mode reading is banked;
- this unit has **real NVS**;
- three of the four attended-window preconditions are already satisfied: login and enable are
  local-only with a known-good privilege-15 account, only privilege 15 is in use, and both PSU
  outlets answer;
- the exact PKI inventory and hostkey fingerprints that the `/flash/.certs → /nvs/.certs` move
  would put at risk — and that there is no rsa1 or dsa key to lose;
- the fifteen documented Normal-vs-secure-mode differences, quoted, with this DUT's starting
  point for each clause of the case title.

**Not established** — the fifteen limbs in §8, every one of them downstream of an enable step
that this unattended window must not take, and unknowns U1 (reboot) and U2 (startup-config),
which no read-only measurement reached.

The grade is **PARTIAL** on that split: the baseline, the CLI surface, the normal-mode `show
post`, the de-risking measurements and the documented consequences are genuine evidence; the
feature's actual behaviour under secure mode is untested.


VERDICT: PARTIAL -- secure mode confirmed disabled and its full CLI surface, normal-mode `show post` and documented differences measured read-only; the enable limb and all 15 downstream checks are NOT RUN, blocked to an attended window by the Test Engineer's instruction and by the measured fact that enabling withdraws the `radius-server local` this campaign is built on.
